From d1618baf12be3b0e1df88870ce29168dafaf9a5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StefanVonRanda <16295563+StefanVonRanda@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:10:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Add the ai-toolkit edit format (--edit-format,
 --vision-pixels): Qwen3.5 vision in the text encoder

Edit LoRAs trained with ai-toolkit (akhaliq/MOSS-Image-Edit-HQ, CharRef) could not be used: they expect the
text encoder to see each reference as "Picture N: <|vision_start|><|image_pad|><|vision_end|>" before the
prompt, and their reference latents on the target's RoPE frame (t = text length), while the engine only had
chinoll's layout (references at t = 0) and its text encoder skipped the vision tower.

- text_encoder.py: VisionTower, a port of mlx-vlm's qwen3_5 (= qwen3_vl) vision model (patch embed as a
  Linear, bilinear position-table resampling, 2-D RoPE, 27 blocks, 2x2 merger), weights from the official
  OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-SFT text_encoder shard 4 (all visual.* keys; the MLX tiers ship none), downloaded on
  first use and run in fp32. Qwen2-VL patch layout and smart_resize (Qwen3.5 preprocessor_config), <|image_pad|>
  expanded per image, vision features scattered into the embeddings, and Qwen3.5's 3-D M-RoPE position ids
  (get_rope_index) with interleaved sections in the reference attention. Text-only prompts take the old path.
- dit.py: edit_format on the forward; ai-toolkit shifts target and text by -L on t so the references stay at
  t = 0 (equivalent to ostris' references at t = L; derivation in the EDIT_FORMATS comment), which keeps one
  reference cache valid for both CFG branches. chinoll unchanged.
- pipeline.py / cli.py: Request.edit_format ("chinoll" default | "ai-toolkit"), Request.vision_pixels
  (147456 = 384^2 default; 262144 for HQ v5); references shown to the encoder scaled down (never up) to that
  many pixels; the negative prompt gets the images too (as ComfyUI-Moss-Image-Edit-Native).
- cache.py: prompt-cache key includes the images' pixels as the tower sees them; text-only keys unchanged.

Checked:
- pytest 50 passed (new: token layout incl. Picture prefix inside the user turn, position ids, M-RoPE
  sections, patch layout, smart_resize, tower shapes, cache key, request fields; DiT with ai-toolkit equals
  the joint sequence with references at t = L for two text lengths, chinoll at t = 0).
- Vision parity on the test image (384^2, 144 tokens), scratch venv with mlx-vlm 0.7.10: processor pixel
  values equal transformers' Qwen2VLImageProcessor (max diff 6e-8); tower vs mlx-vlm both fp32 rel L2 0.0013,
  min token cosine 0.99998; vs transformers fp32 rel 0.0033. In bf16 (mlx-vlm's default) the tower drifts to
  rel 0.053 / min cosine 0.71 against fp32, hence fp32 here. Position ids equal mlx-vlm's get_rope_index.
- Real renders on compact, 1024^2, armV5-moss-edit-lora + 8-step DMD, 8 steps CFG 1, vision 512^2:
  "Change the woman's sundress to a bright red dress" keeps the street and makes the dress red (49 s, MLX
  peak 11.4 GB); the same with 28 steps CFG 3 without DMD (both branches, different text lengths) too
  (399 s, 10.3 GB). chinoll on the same prompt also works (45 s, 11.1 GB).
- Two pictures (fox on grey as picture 2): HQ keeps the scene with no double exposure but does not place the
  fox (purple fragments only; its card says multi-reference compositing is limited), 388 s, 14.3 GB;
  chinoll blends the fox over the woman (195 s, 13.9 GB).

Not checked: full text-encoder hidden states against transformers with images (only the tower, the
token layout and the position ids separately); 50-step CFG 3 HQ; CharRef; non-square references in a render.

